    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1960-p21.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "A square with diagonal \\(a+b\\) has area \\(\\frac{(a+b)^2}{2}.\\) Square II therefore has area \\((a+b)^2,\\) so its side is \\(a+b\\) and its perimeter is \\(4(a+b).\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is E.",
